:: Landing Stage
{<!-- The Lamp at Saltmere, as a Harlowe story: a tiny fixture written for Inkventure (MIT). Built into
   lamp-harlowe.html by scripts/fixtures/build-twine.ts. Walkthrough: take the can, climb, fill, light. -->
(set: $hasCan to false, $filled to false)}
The ferry leaves you on the landing stage of Saltmere. Night is falling, and the lighthouse above the harbour is dark.

A paraffin can stands by the bollard.

(link: "Take the paraffin can")[(set: $hasCan to true)(go-to: "Foot of the Tower")]
[[Walk up to the lighthouse->Foot of the Tower]]

:: Foot of the Tower
The lighthouse door is ajar. A spiral stair climbs into the dark.(if: $hasCan)[ The paraffin can sloshes in your hand.]

[[Climb the stair->Lamp Room]]
[[Read the keeper's log->Keeper's Log]]
[[Wait for morning->The Lamp Stays Dark]]

:: Keeper's Log
The log lies open on a shelf by the door. The last keeper wrote a line for every night of the season.

//October the first.// Wind from the south-west, a heavy swell. Lit the lamp at dusk and trimmed the wick at midnight. The coaster from Harwick passed at two bells, well clear of the Teeth.

//October the second.// Fog until noon. Rang the bell every quarter hour. The paraffin delivery is late again; I have enough for four nights, perhaps five if the weather holds.

//October the third.// Clear and cold. The lens wants polishing. A seal on the landing stage all afternoon, watching the gulls.

//October the fourth.// The delivery came at last. I left the can by the bollard, too tired to carry it up the stair tonight.

//October the fifth.// Nothing more is written. The ink has run where the page got wet.

[[Put the log back->Foot of the Tower]]

:: Lamp Room
The great lamp sits in its brass cradle, its reservoir (if: $filled)[full of paraffin](else:)[dry].

(if: $hasCan and not $filled)[(link: "Fill the lamp")[(set: $filled to true)(go-to: "Lamp Room")]]
(if: $filled)[ [[Light the lamp->The Lamp Is Lit]] ]
[[Go back down->Foot of the Tower]]

:: The Lamp Is Lit
The wick catches, and the beam sweeps out over the water. Far off, a ship's horn answers.

''THE END'': you have lit the lamp.

:: The Lamp Stays Dark
You sit on the step and wait. No ship will find the harbour tonight.

''THE END'': the lamp stays dark.
